WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.334
-Working here at the show is
a lot like camp

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.601
I would say, right?

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.934
There's a lot of activities
throughout the day.

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:07.033
We eat a lot of meals together.
We work long hours,

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:09.534
so people spend a lot of times
away from their families.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:10.968
And we have a lot of fun here,

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:12.467
but it's important
to stay connected.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.167
It's a camp tradition
that everyone

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:15.734
has to write home once a day.

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:16.901
So here at the show,

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.067
we're making letters home
something of a rule.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:21.467
And just like my camp counselors
had to do with me,

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.234
I'm checking in with everybody
else to make sure

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:24.734
that they are all writing
their letters.

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:27.267
So, let's see, Quest -- Quest,
do you have your letter ready?

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.634
-Yeah, here, Jimmy, here.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:31.467
-Oh, cool.
-Hey, Mom.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.834
It's me, Questlove.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:35.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.434
The summer's really been great
so far.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.934
Being the band leader at "The
Tonight Show" is the best job

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:42.267
in the world because I get to
spend all day

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:44.734
playing music with my friends.

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:47.801
The only thing is my bunkmate,
Tariq,

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:51.000
keeps eating all the brownies
you send.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.501
So please send more
and this time with a lock

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:57.467
that only I know
the combination to.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:00.067
Or a box labelled
"maybe poison."

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:01.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:05.767
Also, he snores and he raps
in his sleep too.

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.567
He sleep-raps.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.767
And they're not even that good.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.767
I recorded him last night.

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:14.267
Listen to this.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:17.100
-[ Slowly ] ♪ My name's Tariq
and I'm here to say ♪

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.868
♪ I like to rhyme
in a major way ♪

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:22.868
♪ I can rap like this,
I can rap like that ♪

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:26.434
♪ I can rap me out
because I'm the rapping dog ♪

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:27.667
♪ Hee haw ♪

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:29.801
[ Snoring ]

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:33.067
-Anyway, I miss you guys.

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:35.267
Oh, P.S., I won an Oscar.

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.734
Love, Quest.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.901
-That's a great letter home.
That's a great letter home.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.234
Thank you very much, Quest.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.767
Let's check in with
one of our editors.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.267
Mark, do you have your letter?

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.601
-Sure do.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:52.667
Dear Mom and Dad, I've been
having lots of fun as an editor

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.033
at "The Tonight Show."

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:56.634
But the job can be
pretty stressful.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:02:01.067
I've gone from smoking a pack
a day to smoking a pack an hour.

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:04.968
Sometimes I just put an elastic
band around all the cigarettes

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:08.734
like this and smoke them
all at once.

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.901
It's a lot more efficient.

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:14.167
I guess you could say
I'm some kind of genius.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:18.467
By the way, I'll try to come
home next week for my birthday.

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.767
Can't believe I'm turning 24.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.868
[ Laughter ]
Sincerely, Mark.

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.200
[ Applause ]
-That's so nice.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.834
Oh, that's sweet.

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:30.100
I knew him when he was 21.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:33.133
-Let's check in with one of
our producers, Brian McDonald.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:35.534
Brian, will you please
read your letter?

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:38.534
-Hey, family, it's your favorite
son, Brian.

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:40.634
I'm having a great time
at the show.

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:43.267
But I'm actually writing to tell
you I'm permanently

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.234
changing my name to Ryan.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:48.334
When I started here
over a decade ago, one guy

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.501
called me Ryan in a meeting
and I didn't say anything.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:54.901
And now it's 10 years later and
everyone still calls me Ryan.

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:57.267
It's been so long,
I'm starting to question

00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:59.767
if my real name ever was Brian.

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:00.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.567
Or maybe it was Ivan.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.534
I think I'll just go with Rylan.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:07.067
Yeah, Rylan.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:08.534
See you soon.

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.133
Love, Brian.

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.601
Damn it.
-Alright. Excellent.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.267
[ Applause ]
Excellent job.

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:16.734
Excellent. These are great.

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:20.334
Now let's hear from one of
our writers, Martin.

00:03:20.334 --> 00:03:22.000
Martin, will you please read
your letter?

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.901
-Dear Mom and Dad,

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:27.968
this is the weirdest space camp
I've ever been too.

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:31.734
Nobody ever wears their
astronaut suits except for me.

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:34.367
And any time I ask about
taking the shuttle,

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:37.601
they send me in a Chevy Suburban
to LaGuardia Airport.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:39.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:42.901
I haven't learned a single thing
about the Space Force program

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:45.901
yet, but "The Tonight Show"
announcer, Mr. Steve Higgins,

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:48.901
said that if I was interested,
he could sell me something

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:52.133
that would make me
"feel weightless AF."

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:57.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.534
Sounds fun.

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:01.834
So please send sixty dol--

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:02.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.400
Please send $70 cash.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.934
I love you.
Please send me money.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:08.167
-Thank you, Martin.

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:10.434
Jeff Goldblum is on the show
tonight.

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:12.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:14.634
Jeff, do you have a letter
for us?

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:21.100
-Dearest mater and dear pater,

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.934
things are going well for me
in entertainment.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:27.968
I'm having so much fun being
a guest on

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:29.667
"The Jimmy Fallon Show."

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:32.601
Earlier, Jimmy came to
my dressing room

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.267
and said "hi" to me.

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.567
And then after that,
I said "hi" to him.

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:37.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:42.367
The dressing room had a lot of
nice snacks, like carrots,

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:45.868
celery, those little containers
of hummus

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.667
with the pretzels in the lid.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.834
There were some Triscuits
and cashews,

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:53.033
almonds, even Jordan almonds.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.100
You know them?

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:58.000
They're candy-coated
like a fancy M&amp;M,

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.334
but no chocolate,
not even a little.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:07.067
Despite that, they're still a
tasty treat, a treat best suited

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:12.067
for someone with hard teeth like
a Lorne Greene

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:14.434
or a James Garner.

00:05:14.434 --> 00:05:17.968
Also, "Jurassic World: Dominion"
is coming out soon,

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.634
and I play a character in it.

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:24.968
-I'm glad that everyone's
doing it.

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:27.033
I can't wait to see this.
Thank you, Jeff.

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.267
Of course, I always write home,
too.

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:32.267
And as usual, I'd like to write
a note, please.

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:34.501
I'll use my letter-reading
voice.

00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:37.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:39.601
-Dip that ink.

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:42.400
[ Medieval music plays ]

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.400
-[ British accent ]
To my dearest mumsy and dadsy,

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.434
my deepest and sincerest
apologies.

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:52.667
'Tis been many a fortnight since
I corresponded with thee last,

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:55.300
but I've been terribly busy now
that the new season of

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.734
"Stranger Things" hath dropped.

00:05:57.734 --> 00:06:00.734
Netflix and chilling
I've been indeed.

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:02.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.734 --> 00:06:07.033
As thou might surmise from
the show's curious moniker,

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:11.300
'tis a veritable phantasmagoria
of odd occurrences

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:17.868
befalling a ragtag band of chums
in the year of our Lord 1986.

00:06:17.868 --> 00:06:20.634
Oh, how I meant to phone thee
upon finishing, but I was

00:06:20.634 --> 00:06:25.501
woefully indisposed after
imbibing an entire container of

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:28.968
something called
Mountain Dew Flamin' Hot.

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:32.667
My word, the only stranger
things I've encountered

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:34.601
since that are --

00:06:34.601 --> 00:06:37.200
Sorry.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.534
Can I erase?

00:06:38.534 --> 00:06:40.067
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.067 --> 00:06:42.033
Now, here we go.
-Re-dip.

00:06:42.033 --> 00:06:47.000
-My word, the only stranger
thing I've encountered since

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.734
are what this vile beverage doth
wrought upon my innards.

00:06:50.734 --> 00:06:54.434
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.434 --> 00:06:59.033
Anyway, I hope this latest
missive finds you well.

00:06:59.033 --> 00:07:03.133
I low-key miss you both ever
so much, no cap.

00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:06.834
Your most humblest of sons,
James Tiberious Fallon.

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:08.834
Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:08.834 --> 00:07:10.667
[ Normal voice ]
Those are our "letters home."

00:07:10.667 --> 00:07:13.300
We'll be right back with
Jeff Goldblum, everyone.

